.TH XD\-TIMEDATE 1 2026-10-18 XeonDesktop "XeonDesktop Manual"
.SH NAME
xd\-timedate \- Date and Time Properties
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY xd\-timedate
.OP \-\-page n
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B xd\-timedate
is Windows XP's Date and Time Properties (Control Panel > Date and Time;
double-clicking the taskbar clock):
.TP
.B Date & Time
The month, year and day, an analog clock and the time.
.TP
.B Time Zone
The time zone.
.TP
.B Internet Time
Network time synchronization on or off; with systemd-timesyncd, the
server it uses (from all it knows of: its runtime list, timesyncd.conf,
the network's and the fallback servers) and
.BR "Update Now" ,
which makes it synchronize again and reports the answer.
A server chosen here is given to timesyncd at runtime
.RB ( SetRuntimeNTPServers ,
systemd 255 and later) and lasts until the computer restarts; to keep one,
set
.B NTP=
in
.BR timesyncd.conf (5).
With another time service (chrony, ntpd), only synchronization on or off
is offered.
.PP
Changes go through systemd-timedated
.RB ( org.freedesktop.timedate1 ),
systemd-timesyncd
.RB ( org.freedesktop.timesync1 )
and, for Update Now, systemd (restarting
.BR systemd\-timesyncd.service ),
which ask polkit, so
.BR xd\-polkit (1)
asks for a password when one is needed.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-page " n"
Open on the
.IR n th
tab, from 0 (Date & Time).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR timedatectl (1),
.BR systemd\-timesyncd (8),
.BR xd\-control (1)
